    "background_story": "Dalton was a struggling artist, working multiple part-time jobs to make ends meet while pursuing his passion for painting. One day, while browsing through a local art gallery, he stumbled upon an exhibition of works by the famous artist, Claude Monet. Inspired by the master's impressionist style, Dalton began to experiment with his own techniques, attempting to imitate the soft, dreamy quality of Monet's paintings. As he honed his craft, Dalton's art gained attention from local collectors, who praised his remarkable ability to capture the essence of Monet's style. However, Dalton soon realized that imitation, while a valuable learning tool, was not a substitute for originality. He began to explore his own unique voice, blending his admiration for Monet with his own innovative vision. Dalton's artistic journey became a testament to the power of imitation as a stepping stone to self-discovery and creative growth.",
